@startuml arch-policy-playground
!define RECTANGLE class

skinparam component {
  BackgroundColor<<browser>> LightBlue
  BackgroundColor<<gateway>> LightGreen
  BackgroundColor<<policy>> Pink
  BackgroundColor<<backend>> LightGray
  BorderColor Black
  ArrowColor Black
}

skinparam defaultTextAlignment center

title Policy Playground Architecture\n(API Keys + Rate Limiting)

rectangle "Browser\n(UI)" as browser <<browser>>
rectangle "AWS Load Balancer\n+ OpenShift Router" as router <<gateway>>
rectangle "Gateway\nrhcl-workshop-gw\n- TLS termination\n- Listener: rhcl-workshop.<domain>" as gateway <<gateway>>
rectangle "AuthPolicy (Gateway-level)\n- deny-by-default\n- Zero-trust baseline" as gw_auth <<policy>>
rectangle "HTTPRoute\ndemo-api\n- Path: /hello" as httproute <<gateway>>
rectangle "AuthPolicy (Route-level)\n- API key validation\n- IAMALICE / IAMBOB" as route_auth <<policy>>
rectangle "RateLimitPolicy\n- Identity-based limits\n- Alice: 5 req/10s\n- Bob: 2 req/10s" as ratelimit <<policy>>
rectangle "Backend Service\ndemo-api\n- Pod" as backend <<backend>>

browser -down-> router : "HTTPS Request\nGET /hello\nAPIKEY IAMALICE"
router -down-> gateway : "SNI routing"
gateway -down-> httproute : "Route match"
httproute -down-> backend : "Forward\n(if all policies pass)"

gw_auth -right-> gateway : "applies to\n(deny-all)"
route_auth -right-> httproute : "applies to\n(API key check)"
ratelimit -right-> httproute : "applies to\n(rate limit check)"

note right of gw_auth
**Policy Evaluation Order:**
①Gateway AuthPolicy (deny-all)
②Route AuthPolicy (API key)
③RateLimitPolicy (token count)
④All pass → Forward
⑤Any fail → 401/403/429
end note

note right of backend
**Response Codes:**
• 200 = Success (valid key, under limit)
• 401 = Unauthorized (missing/invalid key)
• 403 = Forbidden (denied by policy)
• 429 = Too Many Requests (rate limit)
end note

@enduml
